<Layout title="Terms — Seven Sins" description="Intended use and limitations of the Seven Sins entertainment personality test, its IPIP questions, scores, and result images."><article class="article-page"><a class="back-home" href="/">← Back to the test</a><h1>A test for reflection.<br/>Not a verdict.</h1><p class="lead">Seven Sins is offered for entertainment and personal reflection. Using the site means understanding the limits below.</p><h2>What this test is for</h2><p>The test uses self-reported answers to public-domain IPIP items and applies our own seven-sin interpretation. It is not a validated assessment, diagnosis, professional advice, or a measure of anyone’s moral character. Do not use it for employment, education admissions, clinical decisions, or decisions about another person’s rights or access to services.</p><h2>Scores and descriptions</h2><p>Results depend on your answers and this version’s scoring rules. They may change over time or with different circumstances. Percentages are test score proportions, not comparisons against a representative population. Descriptions are general reflections and may not fit your life. No result creates a professional relationship or a guarantee of accuracy.</p><h2>Content and sharing</h2><p>IPIP items are public-domain material under the conditions stated by <a href="https://ipip.ori.org/newPermission.htm">IPIP</a>. Our mapping is independent and does not imply endorsement. You may download and share the result image created for you. Share another person’s result only with their permission.</p><h2>Audience and use</h2><p>The questionnaire includes non-graphic statements about sexual desire. It is intended for adults. It is free to take and does not require an account. Use it voluntarily, and stop if you do not wish to answer a statement.</p><h2>Site issues</h2><p>The site is provided as available, and we may correct technical errors or update it. Please <a href="https://github.com/toolution/seven-deadly-sins-test/issues">report a problem</a> if the questionnaire, calculation, or image export does not work as described. These terms describe the version published on November 19, 2026.</p></article></Layout>
